PLAN: {"customer_persona": "Everyday compact-SUV shoppers comparing driving choices, passenger and luggage space, equipment and ownership costs. Their actual routine, location, budget and priorities are unknown until they choose to share them.", "decision_frame": "The strongest fit is a version with the brake-holding, flexible rear seats and front-seat airflow features that matter to you, and the thing still to verify is the exact engine and trim at a current on-road price.", "takeaway": "Choose the engine and trim together, then check the features, personal fit and current quote for that exact version.", "primary_outcome": "Choose a CRETA engine and trim for a personal fit check.", "supporting_outcomes": ["Check which comfort and practical features the chosen version includes.", "Identify the current price and missing ownership evidence before booking."], "concerns": [{"topic": "powertrain", "why": "The three engines have different gearbox choices, while measured acceleration and engine-specific fuel economy are missing.", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F005", "F006", "F008", "F009"]}, {"topic": "space-and-practicality", "why": "Seat flexibility and a pictured boot cannot establish personal passenger, luggage or parking fit.", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F022", "F023", "F063"]}, {"topic": "safety", "why": "The buyer needs to distinguish standard equipment, selected-trim assistance and an as-yet-unverified crash rating.", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F026", "F027", "F028", "F030", "F031", "F034", "F062"]}, {"topic": "ownership", "why": "An entry ex-showroom amount is not a chosen-version on-road quote, and warranty packages cost extra.", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"]}, {"topic": "running-costs", "why": "No approved fuel-economy measurement, service cost or resale evidence is supplied.", "fact_ids": []}], "usps": [{"id": "rest-at-a-stop", "name": "Rest your foot at a stop", "fact_ids": ["F015", "F016"], "stop_id": "powertrain"}, {"id": "room-for-changing-plans", "name": "Make room for changing plans", "fact_ids": ["F022", "F023"], "stop_id": "space-and-practicality"}, {"id": "relief-from-the-heat", "name": "A little relief from the heat", "fact_ids": ["F037", "F038"], "stop_id": "delighters"}], "segments": [{"id": "overview", "title": "The button beside the brake", "role": "intro", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Preview the first stop through a possible pause in stop-start driving, without assigning that routine to this buyer. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Use F015\u2013F016 for the stationary brake-holding function on equipped versions, with King, King Knight and Lounge standard and S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatic-only availability held beside the claim; leave engine figures for powertrain detail. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on the AUTO HOLD button in im11 and leave the button in focus, using 35 words in one batch with no closing statement.", "outcome": "", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": ["rest-at-a-stop"], "visual_refs": ["im11"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 35}, {"id": "remember", "title": "The brake button, rear seats and front seats", "role": "outcome", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Give three memorable anchors for a tour the buyer can steer by interrupting. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Name exactly the three reviewed USPs, using F015\u2013F016 for brake holding on equipped trims, F022\u2013F023 for the standard split rear seat, and F037\u2013F038 for front-seat airflow on SX Premium, King, King Knight and Lounge; keep the full availability details for their stops. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start with the AUTO HOLD button in im11, change to the folded split seats in im13, then the airflow illustration in im21, ending on the seats within 43 words and without a closing statement.", "outcome": "Choose which everyday features matter", "topic": "highlights", "fact_ids": ["F015", "F016", "F022", "F023", "F037", "F038"], "usp_ids": ["rest-at-a-stop", "room-for-changing-plans", "relief-from-the-heat"], "visual_refs": ["im11", "im13", "im21"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 43}, {"id": "driving", "title": "The brake button and engine choices", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Start with the labelled brake button and a possible stop on the drive home, then explore which engine and gearbox combination to try. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F015\u2013F016 as holding the stationary vehicle without keeping the brake pressed on equipped versions, explicitly identifying standard fit on King, King Knight and Lounge and reserving S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatic-only details for deeper; use F003, F005\u2013F006, F008\u2013F009 for separate petrol, diesel and turbo-petrol choices, manual or automatic for the first two subject to trim and automatic-only turbo listed only on King, while F004 and F007 stay deeper with their complete stated power or torque units and engine-speed basis, and F002 remains manufacturer positioning rather than a tested result. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on im11, switch to im06, im05 and im04 as the separate engines are discussed and im07 only for the manual lever, leave the engine/gearbox choice in focus, and allocate 90 words across three batches of about 30 each with no closing statement.", "outcome": "Choose an engine combination to try", "topic": "powertrain", "fact_ids": ["F002", "F003", "F004", "F005", "F006", "F007", "F008", "F009", "F015", "F016"], "usp_ids": ["rest-at-a-stop"], "visual_refs": ["im04", "im05", "im06", "im07", "im11"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "powertrain", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 90}, {"id": "wheels", "title": "The wheels meeting the road", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the alloy wheel and distinguish its visible design from how it might feel on a particular road. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Use F017 to explain that wheel choices change by trim, keeping the complete F017 trim mapping and F064 tyre-size specifications in deeper; ground clearance, suspension and comparative rough-road comfort remain unanswered and wheel size establishes none of them. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open and stay on the literal wheel and tyre close-up im12, with im02 available for the whole-car context, leaving the wheel as the subject for 24 words in one batch without a closing statement.", "outcome": "Check wheel choice and road feel", "topic": "stance-and-ride", "fact_ids": ["F017", "F064"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im01", "im02", "im03", "im12"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "stance-and-ride", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 24}, {"id": "space", "title": "The rear seat and open boot", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the differently sized folded seatbacks and explore a possible day with passengers and luggage without assuming their number or bags. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F022\u2013F023 for the standard split rear seat and its passenger/storage trade-off, F001 for five seats if needed, and F063 as the manufacturer-stated boot purpose followed by a personal luggage fit-check; hold F020, F021, F024, F059\u2013F061 and the exact split ratio in deeper, preserving rear vents and armrest as standard, rear recline from S(O), rear shades from EX(O), and sliding front armrest only on King, King Knight and Lounge, with no invented boot litres or legroom. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on folded rear seats im13, switch to the visible sample bags in im15 without promising they match the buyer\u2019s luggage, and leave the open boot in focus across 52 words in two batches, ending with a short statement that the buyer\u2019s own bags are the useful fit check.", "outcome": "Check passenger and luggage fit", "topic": "space-and-practicality", "fact_ids": ["F001", "F020", "F021", "F022", "F023", "F024", "F059", "F060", "F061", "F063"], "usp_ids": ["room-for-changing-plans"], "visual_refs": ["im13", "im14", "im15", "im31"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "space-and-practicality", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 52}, {"id": "protection", "title": "The airbags around the seats", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Look at where the illustrated airbags sit before separating equipment fitted to every version from extra assistance. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F025 for six airbags across the range and F031\u2013F032 with F034 for collision warning and assistance on King, King Knight and Lounge while retaining driver responsibility; keep F026\u2013F030, F033, F035\u2013F036 and F062 deeper with standard stability control, disc brakes, hill-start help, tyre-pressure monitoring and rear sensors, cameras on SX Premium/King/King Knight/Lounge, and adaptive stop-go only on automatics of King/King Knight/Lounge, without inferring crash ratings, stopping distance or guaranteed intervention. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start with the deployed-airbag illustration im16, use im18 for the forward detection illustration and im19 or im20 only for their literal subjects in deeper answers, leaving forward assistance in focus over 58 words in two batches with no closing statement.", "outcome": "Distinguish standard protection and assistance", "topic": "safety", "fact_ids": ["F025", "F026", "F027", "F028", "F029", "F030", "F031", "F032", "F033", "F034", "F035", "F036", "F062"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im16", "im17", "im18", "im19", "im20"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "safety", "fundamental": true, "word_budget": 58}, {"id": "comfort", "title": "Airflow through the front seats", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Consider returning to a hot parked car as a possible situation, noticing the airflow arrows through the seats before the roof and speakers. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F037\u2013F038 for cool airflow through the front-seat cushions on SX Premium, King, King Knight and Lounge, F048\u2013F049 for the panoramic roof from EX(O) and voice opening/closing from SX, and F050 for Bose sound on SX Premium, King, King Knight and Lounge; keep the eight-speaker specification deeper and do not claim a cooling time, refrigerated air or improved driving safety. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on seat-airflow illustration im21, change to im27 or im26 for the roof and im25 for the speaker layout, and leave speakers in focus within 53 words in two batches without a closing statement.", "outcome": "Choose seat airflow roof and sound", "topic": "delighters", "fact_ids": ["F037", "F038", "F048", "F049", "F050"], "usp_ids": ["relief-from-the-heat"], "visual_refs": ["im21", "im25", "im26", "im27"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "delighters", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 53}, {"id": "controls", "title": "The temperature controls and phone connection", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the two temperature settings and consider a driver and front passenger wanting different settings. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F039\u2013F040 for independent front temperature settings from S(O) and F045\u2013F046 for compatible Android Auto or Apple CarPlay from EX, explicitly keeping the wired-to-wireless adapter condition on SX and above; hold F041\u2013F044 and F047 deeper with both 26.03 cm (10.25-inch) screens from SX, Bluelink from SX with three complimentary years and 70+ features subject to power/network, Alexa Home to Car from SX with separate hardware excluded and no inferred phone-app engine start, and both front power seats plus driver memory only on King/King Knight/Lounge. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Open on the literal climate panel im23, move to dashboard im22 as contextual imagery for connectivity rather than a demonstrated wireless link, and use im24 only for memory-button detail, leaving the screen in focus over 50 words in two batches with no closing statement.", "outcome": "Check controls and phone compatibility", "topic": "cabin-and-tech", "fact_ids": ["F039", "F040", "F041", "F042", "F043", "F044", "F045", "F046", "F047"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im22", "im23", "im24"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": "cabin-and-tech", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 50}, {"id": "cost", "title": "The price of your chosen version", "role": "proof", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Turn the feature choices into the cost of a specific engine and trim rather than treating the entry price as a personal quote. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Voice F055\u2013F056 for road tax, registration and insurance added to the ex-showroom amount and the need for a current dealer quotation; keep F054 deeper with the dated 19 September 2026 body price of \u20b910,90,700, conflicting \u20b910.79 lakh structured data and entry ex-showroom basis all together, while F057\u2013F058 warranty detail belongs to the ownership wrap and deeper answers. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Use the whole-car profile im02 only as explicitly contextual imagery because no price or terms document image exists, leave the chosen version in focus for 26 words in one batch, and close with a short statement that a current itemised quote settles the price.", "outcome": "Get the exact on-road quote", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F054", "F055", "F056", "F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im02"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": "ownership", "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 26}, {"id": "small-touches", "title": "Lights by the doors and storage by your seat", "role": "features", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Notice the light beside the door, then two small details inside. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Plan three brief feature sentences from F051\u2013F052 for driver-side puddle lighting from SX and both sides on King/King Knight/Lounge, F061 for standard front-armrest storage, and F013 for Normal, Eco and Sport on King automatics; retain the full selected-automatic trim list, its absent current S(O) Knight automatic combination and Snow/Mud/Sand labels in deeper without claiming off-road capability, and reserve sliding armrest availability for King/King Knight/Lounge. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Start with the literal light pool im28, change to open armrest storage im31 and the drive-mode display im09, leaving the display in focus within 32 words in one batch and no closing statement.", "outcome": "Notice three useful equipment details", "topic": "features", "fact_ids": ["F051", "F052", "F061", "F013"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im28", "im31", "im09"], "priority_topic": false, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 32}, {"id": "ownership-checks", "title": "Your version and the remaining checks", "role": "establish", "goal": "MOMENT \u2014 Keep the engine and trim together when turning interest into a next step. SPOKEN / DEEPER \u2014 Briefly refer to variant choice using F003 and F006, state under F057\u2013F058 that the extended warranty is separately paid and petrol-only while reserving the up-to-seven-years limit and absent package prices/coverage for deeper, and name three unresolved questions with owners: official engine-specific fuel-economy documentation for U002, the applicable model/year crash-test report for U005, and the selected dealer\u2019s stock and delivery confirmation for U009. VISUAL / HANDOFF \u2014 Hold im03 as contextual imagery of a King rather than proof of any price, policy, rating or availability, leave the version to verify in focus, and use 42 words in one batch without a closing statement.", "outcome": "Know what remains to verify", "topic": "ownership", "fact_ids": ["F003", "F006", "F057", "F058"], "usp_ids": [], "visual_refs": ["im03"], "priority_topic": true, "stop_id": null, "fundamental": false, "word_budget": 42}], "ctas": [{"id": "dealer-request", "label": "Request dealer contact", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": true, "when": "end"}, {"id": "test-drive-request", "label": "Request a test drive", "kind": "contact", "url": "", "primary": false, "when": "end"}], "voice": {"persona_name": "Priya", "persona_description": "The guide is a practical, attentive Hyundai product guide. The guide speaks warmly, explains equipment in ordinary words and states what needs checking without pressure.", "tone": "Warm and cheerful Indian English, with short thoughts, restrained pauses and quiet enthusiasm for useful details.", "sample_line": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "suggested_voice": "priya", "language": "en-IN"}, "intake": {"q1": "Hi, welcome to the Hyundai CRETA; would you like to share what you\u2019re looking for in your next car, or shall we get started?", "q2": "", "chips": [{"key": "powertrain", "label": "Driving choices"}, {"key": "stance-and-ride", "label": "Wheels and roads"}, {"key": "space-and-practicality", "label": "Seats and bags"}, {"key": "safety", "label": "Safety equipment"}, {"key": "delighters", "label": "Seat airflow and roof"}, {"key": "cabin-and-tech", "label": "Controls and phone"}, {"key": "ownership", "label": "Price and ownership"}]}, "do_not_recommend_if": "Do not recommend a specific version if a non-negotiable requirement depends on missing fuel-economy, crash-rating, fit, cost or availability evidence until the appropriate source resolves it.", "advance": "When the buyer is ready to verify a version, offer Request dealer contact so the selected Hyundai dealer can confirm the engine and trim and provide a current itemised on-road quotation; the app records this contact preference and optional follow-up, not a completed contact or booking.", "notes": "Unknown customer context: use a balanced route and accept interruptions without a second intake. Copy the Coach\u2019s seven stops and three USPs unchanged; no playbook version was supplied. Guided allocation is 427 words across proof, features and establish, plus 23 words for the Explore overview and 45 for closing, totalling 495; the separate Browse intro/outcome use 78 words and do not consume that guided budget. Only space and cost receive brief declarative checkins; none waits for a reply. Each proof stop uses at most three delivery batches and each batch stays at or below 46 words; features uses 32 of 48 and establish 42 of 44. The configured Sarvam Priya identity is retained. Use ordinary feature explanations in main narration, complete units and source bases in deeper answers, and no calculated performance or economic differences. The ownership stop lacks literal evidence imagery, so contextual treatment and the gap are explicit. The empty-URL CTAs are contact requests because no action destination was supplied. Buyer-specific closing language remains conditional until the buyer actually shares a priority.", "total_words": 495, "playbook_version": "2026-09-23", "guided_minimum_seconds": 180.0, "guided_opening_words": 23, "narration_preparation": {"version": 1, "target_words": 495, "identity": "e4368858179b4941dce1e9b3cf4c8eb6e2e57eb4f9167a9186a6b182d6543a5d"}}

FACT REGISTRY — the only allowed source of facts:
F001 [spec·stated] Body and driveline: five-door, five-seat compact SUV (conditions: All variants; manufacturer compilation dated 19 September 2026) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "The Hyundai CRETA is a five-door, five-seat compact SUV built by Hyundai Motor India and sold with front-wheel\ndrive across the whole range.")
F002 [claim·stated] Intended use: city use while still being capable on longer runs (conditions: Manufacturer positioning; not measured superiority) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 3; quote: "Hyundai positions the car as an SUV that works for city use while still being capable on longer runs.")
F003 [spec·stated] Engine choice: 1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 4; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol; 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol")
F004 [spec·stated] Turbo maximum power: 117.5 kW (160 PS) @ 5,500 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol; specification, not an acceleration measurement) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min")
F005 [spec·stated] Turbo transmission: 7-speed DCT (conditions: Turbo petrol only; DCT means dual-clutch automatic) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l Turbo GDi petrol\n1,482 cm³\n117.5 kW (160 PS) @\n5,500 r/min\n253 Nm (25.8 kgm) @\n1,500–3,500 r/min\n7-speed DCT")
F006 [availability·stated] Turbo trim availability: King (conditions: Column headers E, EX, EX(O), S(O), S(O) Knight, SX, SX Premium, King, King Knight, Lounge Edition. Only King is marked for turbo/DCT. King also offers other engines; do not imply every King is turbo.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 31; quote: "1.5 l turbo GDi petrol\nDCT\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n –\n ●\n –\n –")
F007 [spec·stated] Diesel torque: 250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @ 1,500–2,750 r/min (conditions: 1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel; not a loaded-climb performance test) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min")
F008 [spec·stated] Diesel transmission choices: 6-speed manual or 6-speed automatic (conditions: Trim combinations differ; see engine matrix page 31) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l U2 CRDi diesel\n1,493 cm³\n85 kW (116 PS) @ 4,000\nr/min\n250 Nm (25.5 kgm) @\n1,500–2,750 r/min\n6-speed manual or\n6-speed automatic")
F009 [spec·stated] Petrol transmission choices: 6-speed manual or IVT (conditions: Naturally aspirated petrol; trim combinations differ) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "1.5 l MPi petrol\n1,497 cm³\n84.4 kW (115 PS) @ 6,300\nr/min\n143.8 Nm (14.7 kgm) @ 4,500\nr/min\n6-speed manual or IVT")
F010 [claim·stated] Turbo manufacturer driving description: impressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling (conditions: Hyundai marketing description, not a measured test result; never imply an acceleration time or guaranteed overtaking) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It delivers\nimpressive power, smooth acceleration, and responsive handling for a thrilling yet refined drive across city roads and\nhighways alike")
F011 [claim·stated] Diesel manufacturer driving description: strong torque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance (conditions: Hyundai marketing, not mileage or noise measurements) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "The robust 1.5L U2 CRDi diesel engine, available with 6-speed manual and automatic transmissions, delivers strong\ntorque, high fuel efficiency, and quiet performance.")
F012 [claim·stated] Petrol manufacturer use description: everyday practicality with refined driving comfort (conditions: Hyundai marketing. Do not convert superior fuel economy to a comparative test or mileage figure.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 16; quote: "It combines everyday practicality with refined driving comfort, ensuring consistent\npower delivery and superior fuel economy.")
F013 [feature·stated] Drive and traction modes by trim: Normal, Eco, Sport; Snow, Mud and Sand (conditions: Automatic cars only in the listed trims; no automatic SX listed in engine matrix; S(O) Knight matrix has no current automatic combination) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 17; quote: "Drive mode select and the Snow, Mud and Sand traction control modes are fitted to automatic cars only, and appear on S(O), S(O) Knight, SX\nPremium, King, King Knight and Lounge Edition.")
F014 [feature·stated] Paddle shifters function: quick gear changes (conditions: Automatic cars on S(O), S(O) Knight, SX Premium, King, King Knight, Lounge Edition per p39 starred row. Manufacturer function description; do not imply measured shift time.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 17; quote: "Mounted behind the steering wheel, the paddle shifters enable quick gear changes for enhanced control and sporty\nperformance, making every drive more responsive and enjoyable.")
F015 [feature·stated] Auto hold function: holding the vehicle in place when stationary (conditions: Electronic parking brake with auto hold. S(O), S(O) Knight and SX Premium automatics; King, King Knight and Lounge standard per p39. No guarantee on all surfaces.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 44; quote: "automatically holding the vehicle in place when stationary, eliminating the need to\nkeep the brake pressed.")
F016 [availability·stated] Auto hold applicability: Electric parking brake with auto hold (conditions: E, EX, EX(O): unavailable. S(O), S(O) Knight, SX Premium: automatic only. SX: unavailable. King, King Knight, Lounge: standard. Footnote * = IVT, AT or DCT only, p41.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 39; quote: "Electric parking brake with auto hold\n –\n –\n –\n S*\n S*\n –\n S*\n S\n S\n S")
F017 [spec·stated] Wheel sizes by trim: R16, R17 and R18 (conditions: No comparative ride comfort or road-absorption claim follows from wheel size.) (source: src_reviewed_creta_pdf; locator: PDF page 8; quote: "R16 steel with wheel cover\nE, EX\nR16 dual-tone styled steel\nEX(O)\nR17 black alloys\nS(O)\nR17 diamond cut alloys\nSX, SX Premium\nR18 diamond cut alloys\nKing\nR18 matte black alloys\nS(O) Knight, King Knight, Lounge Edition")
